BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Green Machine w/ Tumbleweed Soul Duo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T223000
UID:261014C_OG7CNLDEyJN7Hx01V01w
DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n\nDoors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10
 :30pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$3 off each ticket when you 
 use the code earlybird15 at checkout. Offer ends October 11th.\n\nPromo
  Codes are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitive\,
  but must be typed as one word.\n\nThe Green Machine is a Petaluma-based t
 rio playing what we call “Garage Americana.” We are rooted in classic 
 country and 60s rock\; inspired by songwriters like Merle Haggard and Gram
  Parsons and groups like the Stones\, Creedence and the Byrds. Adam Walsh 
 and Stephanie Salva\, Tumbleweed Soul Duo\, are best known for their joint
  role in the beloved Sonoma County band the Jug Dealers. With powerful har
 monies and eclectic songwriting that is both familiar yet fresh\, their gr
 owing catalogue of original songs reflects their love of the deep city juk
 e joints and country shacks where Americana was born. www.thegreenmachineb
 and.com Tumbleweed Soul is an American Roots project based in the San Fran
 cisco North Bay\, led by Adam Walsh and Stephanie Salva. The pair have bee
 n rocking the West Coast music scene in various projects for over a decade
 \, best known for their joint role in the beloved Sonoma County band the J
 ug Dealers.  Joining them is Mike Dipirro on bass \\(Free Peoples\, The T
 richromes\\)\, and bay area legend\, Greg Anton on drums \\(Zero\, The Roc
 k Collection\\). With powerful harmonies and eclectic songwriting that is 
 both familiar yet fresh\, their growing catalogue of original songs reflec
 ts their love of the deep city juke joints and country shacks where Americ
 ana was born.  Jazz\, Blues\, Soul\, R&B\, Country\, Funk\, and Old Timey
  Traditionals all find a home at a Tumbleweed show. tumbleweedsoul.com
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 0000CbqlVMAR
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cotati Fall Festival at the Veronda-Falletti Ranch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T160000
UID:261013eZAk9tZ1CUusThW0aYVywg
DESCRIPTION:Come on down for our 4th Annual Cotati Fall Festival!\n\nFesti
 val Details -\n\nDate: Oct 17\n\nTimes: 10:00 am - 4:00 pm\n\nSensory Frie
 ndly Hour - 10:00am - 11:00am\n\nGeneral Admission - 11:00am-4:00pm\n\nLoc
 ation: Veronda-Falletti Ranch\, 175 West Sierra Avenue\, Cotati\n\nFee: $6
  per person over 2 - pre-registration\, $8 at the gate\n\nRegistration enc
 ouraged and will save a lot of time at the gate but drop ins are welcome.
  \n\nAll ages welcome!\n\nChildren 2 and under are free and do not need t
 heir own registration.\n\nRegister online at: https://cotati.recdesk.com/C
 ommunity/Program/Detail?programId=1290\n\nLive music & entertainment by "F
 armer" Arann Harris \\(11am-12pm\\) and Hannah Jern-Miller \\(1pm to 4pm\\
 )\n\nAll-Day Stations include:\n\nPumpkin patch\n\nPumpkin painting\n\nHay
  bale pyramid\n\nSensory bins\n\nGames & crafts\n\nFarm stand - farm grown
  flower bouquets\, dried flowers\, fresh produce\, pumpkins\n\nVisits with
 e the animals\n\nConcession Stand\n\nAnd more!\n\nCome visit our pumpkin p
 atch. Children get to pick a pumpkin to decorate and take home\, participa
 te in games and crafts\, enjoy the live music and entertainment\, visit th
 e animals and enjoy some yummy treats. Many photo opportunities will be av
 ailable.\n\nWe recommend closed toe shoes.\n\n\\*Sensory Friendly hour wil
 l be from 10am-11am. This hour will have limited space available\, no loud
  or live music\, and lots of opportunities for sensory play.\n\nTickets to
  Sensory Friendly Hour: https://cotati.recdesk.com/Community/Program/Deta
 il?programId=1438\n\nIf have questions\, please feel free to reach out to 
 us via email at awilson@cotaticity.gov or 707-665-4222.
LOCATION:Veronda-Falletti Ranch
URL:https://cotati.recdesk.com/Community/Program/Detail?programId=1290
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4th Annual NAMIWalks Sonoma County
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T130000
UID:261013XgsE-xckMk2ZvaoufOPaBA
DESCRIPTION:Help us show that mental health is a priority.\n\nNAMI Sonoma 
 County strives to make our communities a place where everyone who  experi
 ences mental health challenges\, whether as an individual or as a family m
 ember\, friend or caregiver\, recognizes the warning signs\, can access ne
 eded  care and support\, and knows where to ask for help if needed. Help 
 us grow awareness and build a caring community. It’s free and open to al
 l!\n\nHere’s what to expect on October 17th:\n\nGet to know over 20 comm
 unity mental health organizations.\n\nEnjoy live music from the Russian Ri
 ver Ramblers.\n\nHonor a loved one or your own journey at our “Why I Wa
 lk” table. \n\nChoose to walk or just hang out and enjoy! \n\nTake yo
 ur chances on wonderful raffle prizes!\n\nEnjoy activities for kids and ki
 ds at heart.\n\nCuddle with a PALS support dog!\n\nBring your water bottle
  and your friendly\, leashed dog.\n\nFor over 40 years\, NAMI Sonoma Count
 y has provided free mental health education\, support\, awareness and advo
 cacy to our communities.  Your presence will help us to raise both fundin
 g that keeps our programs free of cost to participants and creates awarene
 ss.\n\nRegister at www.namiwalks.org/sonomacounty.\n\nSee you on OCtober 1
 7th!
LOCATION:Howarth Park - Cypress Point A picnic area
URL:https://namiwalks.org/sonomacounty
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Using AI to Bring Your Presentation to Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T140000
UID:2610133vcm1R-LakqYw7azz3XGNQ
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Presents\n\n Using AI t
 o Bring Your Presentation to Life\n\n Presented by Jane Pritchard\n\n Jane
  will present the slide show she created for the Santa Rosa Chapter of the
  DAR honoring her Revolutionary War patriot\, Margaret Eskridge Kenner\, w
 ho supported Revolutionary troops with food and supplies. Along the way sh
 e taught herself to use AI assistants Claude and Nano Banana\, to speed up
  research and to build both the PowerPoint and a companion PDF. She will w
 alk through the simple\, practical ways she used AI — and where it fell 
 short so members can try the same approach with their own ancestors.\n\nJa
 ne began serious family research in 2021\, during the pandemic\, and has s
 ince taken many genealogy classes through Santa Rosa Junior College. She w
 as surprised to discover that her ancestors played a part in the founding 
 of this country — a history her family had never known. That research le
 d to her recent membership in the DAR\, where she now serves on the chapte
 r's Lineage Research Committee helping prospective members document their 
 lines. A native of West Virginia\, Jane has lived in Santa Rosa since 1981
 . She is a mother and grandmother and has practiced as a Jin Shin Jyutsu a
 cupressure therapist for 36 years.\n\n Saturday\, October 17th\n\n Meeti
 ng starts at 12:30 pm\, presentation starts at 1:00 pm PST\n\nMeeting Deta
 ils : The meeting is held via Zoom. Login begins at 12:30 p.m.\n\n FREE V
 ia ZOOM\n\n Register at https://www.scgsonline.org\n\n Registration clos
 es Friday\,  October 16th
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
