BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Sonoma County Writers Conference
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T173000
UID:260803ZE12AP77QUSvUdFwUH7WeQ
DESCRIPTION:Registration is now open for the 2026 Sonoma County Writers Co
 nference!\n\nDear Bay Area Writers and Authors:\n\nWant to become a better
  writer\, or finally turn that idea you've been sitting on for years into 
 your first book? Trying to get noticed in a sea of indie and self-publishe
 d authors? Looking to sharpen your craft\, or just wanting to spend a day 
 with fellow creatives who get it? Whether you're holding your first blank 
 page or your tenth published book\, you're welcome here.\n\nWe invite you 
 to join us for the largest writing conference in the North Bay this fall 
 — a full day of craft\, publishing\, and marketing sessions with practic
 al tools you can start using immediately\, led by working authors and indu
 stry pros\, plus a keynote from award-winning indie poet\, historical nove
 list\, and forensic historian Gini Grossenbacher.\n\nHosted by Redwood Wri
 ters\, the largest branch of the California Writers Club — writers helpi
 ng writers\, at every stage of the page. No matter where you are in your w
 riting life\, there's a seat for you here.\n\nOUR PROMISE: By the end of t
 he day\, you'll have new skills\, new connections\, and the confidence to 
 put them to work.\n\nThis conference is open to writers and authors at any
  level\, whether a member of CWC or not.\n\nSee below for the full registr
 ation details.\n\n\\*Early bird pricing through 9/15/26 — includes conti
 nental breakfast\, snacks\, and lunch\n\n\\*Ample Free Parking.\n\nWe look
  forward to meeting you\, and helping you take your next steps forward on 
 your writing journey.\n\nSincerely\,\n\nShawn Langwell\, 2026 Sonoma Count
 y Writers Conference Chair
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Claire Wells - Violin with pianist Elizabeth Dorman
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T210000
UID:2607157-L291EVeEeSVEf3T-sWYg
DESCRIPTION:American violinist Claire Wells\, born in 2001\, is acclaimed 
 by audiences and the press for her expressive musicality and rich\, singin
 g quality of sound. Solo concert engagements have brought her to halls lik
 e the Wigmore Hall\, the Meyerson Symphony Center\, Bass Performance Hall\
 , Teatro Degollado\, and Konzerthaus Berlin. Wells plays on a Giovanni Bat
 tista Guadagnini\, on loan from a generous donor. Having won major prizes 
 in international competitions\, Claire Wells is the Mendelssohn-Prize 1st 
 Prize winner and Commission Prize winner at the Felix Mendelssohn Barthold
 y Competition 2021\, 2nd Prize winner at the Michael Hill International Vi
 olin Competition 2023\, and has taken major prizes at the Indianapolis Int
 ernational Competition\, Mirecourt International Competition\, Lynn Harrel
 l Competition\, among others. Claire Wells grew up in a musical family\, p
 laying both violin and piano from the age of three. She studied privately 
 with Brian Lewis\, Sandy Yamamoto\, and Emanuel Borok\, and in 2017 attend
 ed the Yehudi Menuhin School with Lutsia Ibragimova. In 2020\, Claire Well
 s studied with Mihaela Martin at the Hochschule für Musik und Tanz Köln.
  Wells has performed with major orchestras such as the Dallas Symphony Orc
 hestra\, Konzerthausorchester Berlin\, the Fort Worth Symphony Orchestra\,
  the Belgrade Philharmonic Orchestra\, the Jalisco Philharmonic\, the Shen
  Zhen Symphony Orchestra\, among others. A passionate chamber musician\, C
 laire Wells has worked alongside majoartists such as Enrico Pace\, Nobuko 
 Imai\, Frans Helmerson\, Christian Tetzlaff\, and Steven Isserlis. Wells h
 as also taken coachings from the likes of Ana Chumachenco\, Boris Kuschnir
 \, Andras Schiff and Robert Levin. Claire Wells has performed at festivals
  such as the International Holland Music Sessions\, Music@Menlo chamber mu
 sic festival\, Chamber Music Connects the World\, Gstaad Festival\, the Ve
 rbier Festival\, and others.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/claire-wells-violin-with-pianist-eliz
 abeth-dorman/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
