DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T200000
UID:261013Dxk-rJxkxkWtynYdewiPJg
DESCRIPTION:Experience Día de los Muertos through another form of storyte
 lling: the spoken and written word. \n\n\n\nSaturday\, October 17  6 pm 
 – 8 pm\n\nPetaluma Historical Library & Museum\n\n20 4th Street \\(Corne
 r of 4th & B Street\\)\n\nFree\n\nReserve A Spot\n\nJoin us for an evening
  of poetry\, memory\, and reflection surrounded by the community ofrendas 
 of the Petaluma Museum’s annual Día de los Muertos exhibition\, present
 ed in partnership with El Día de los Muertos Petaluma. \n\nPoetry of Reme
 mbrance brings voices together to explore love\, loss\, ancestry\, memory\
 , and the many ways we keep those who came before us present in our lives.
  \n\nThe evening offers a beautiful opportunity to experience Día de los 
 Muertos through another form of storytelling: the spoken and written word.
  \n\nCome listen\, reflect\, and share in an evening centered on the endur
 ing power of memory and connection. \n\nPresented in partnership with El D
 ía de los Muertos Petaluma. \n\nAll are welcome.
LOCATION:Petaluma Historical Library and Museum
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/poesia-del-recuerdo-poet
 ry-of-remembrance/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
