BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senderos & Rutas y Aventuras: Retos en las montañas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T150000
UID:260930aZ2JMOpvIUGdlF5irupfgg
DESCRIPTION:\\[Translated to English Below\\] Este otoño\, acompaña a gu
 ías de Jack London Park Partners y Sonoma Ecology Center en una series de
  caminatas de nivel intermediario que intercambiarán entre Jack London St
 ate Historic Park y Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Las excursiones serán pri
 mariamente los sábados 10\, 17\, y 24 de octubre\, el 7 y 21 de noviembre
 \, y el domingo 15 de noviembre\, y cada una aumentará en dificultad o du
 ración\, por la cual no son apropiadas para niños menores de 12 años.\n
 \nEvento gratuito\; requiere registración. Hay transportación disponible
  gratuita dentro de un radio de 20 millas al parque para familias que la n
 ecesiten. Para detalles y registración\, visita https://sec.regfox.com/re
 to2026 \n\nAlternativamente\, llama a (Carlos: 707-938-5216\, ext 9\; Mar
 io 707-387-4087\; Alma 707-247-5767)\, entre martes y sábado) o escríben
 os a senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org. ¿No puedes acompañarnos para este
  evento? ¡Guarda la fecha el 11 de octubre para más aventuras!\n\nSender
 os Naturales es parcialmente respaldado por una beca de Parks California.\
 n\nFotografía cortesía de Alma Shaw\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_
 \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nEnglish: This fall\, join Jack London Park 
 Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff in a 6-week series of intermediat
 e hikes between Jack London State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State 
 Park. The hikes will be primarily on Saturdays\, October 10\, 17\, and 24\
 , and November 7 and 21\, with the exception of Sunday\, November 15\, and
  they will switch parks back and forth. Each hike will increase in length 
 or difficulty\, which does not make this series appropriate for children u
 nder 12 years old. \n\nThis event is planned around a primarily Latino au
 dience\, but all are welcome to this bilingual hiking series.\n\nFamilies 
 from underrepresented groups are welcome to join. Free transportation avai
 lable within a 20 mile radius of the park for families in need. For questi
 ons\, please email senderos@sonomaecologycenter.org.\n\nThis event is part
 ially supported by Route to Parks\, a project of Parks California.\n\nPhot
 o Courtesy of Alma Shaw
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Beauty Ranch Meadow\, Sugarloaf
  Ridge State Park\, Kenwood\, CA
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/reto2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T170000
UID:2609149KMrKa9GAkykpzkRSdvPOg
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present “Antarctica: The F
 rozen Desert\,” a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\, o
 pening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November.  T
 he exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after m
 ore than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity\,
  he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar regio
 ns. The exhibit features work generated over 6 voyages to the Antarctic Pe
 ninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Falklan
 ds and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photograph.\
 n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on Ear
 th\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely out
 side of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of year
 s ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 years. D
 efined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — vast
 \, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a kind
  of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever before
 .
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maple Magic & Winter Wonder
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T170000
UID:260824ciOFVRKgGUSCRZrka6n7xA
DESCRIPTION:As the days grow shorter and cooler\, Sonoma Botanical Garden 
 transforms with the beauty of the changing seasons. From the first signs o
 f autumn in October to the brilliant display of rare Asian maples in Nov
 ember and the quiet beauty of early winter in December\, each visit offer
 s something new to discover. \n\nMaple Magic & Winter Wonder invites vis
 itors to experience this special time of year through nature\, creativity\
 , and connection. Throughout the season\, the Garden offers guided walks\,
  hands-on workshops\, lectures\, and special experiences inspired by the c
 hanging landscape. Wander among vibrant fall foliage\, breathe in the swee
 t fragrance of katsura trees\, enjoy creative programs\, and experience th
 e peaceful beauty of the Garden as it transitions into winter.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/maple-magic-winter-wonder/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Park Rx—Intermediate Hiking for Fitness Fall 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T130000
UID:260823_3qiDNnPqUOeQIQT5GLApA
DESCRIPTION:The program leaders will guide you on 8 weekly hikes
  with the challenge increasing each week. Leaders will have grou
 p discussions about gear\, hydration\, hiking poles\, first aid a
 nd pacing\, etc. The group's final hike aims for Bald Mountain\,
  where hikers can enjoy stunning vistas.\n\nThe following is a l
 ist of possible routes specifically selected for this hiking seri
 es: \n\n1) Sat 9/26 — Creekside + Waterfall loop\, 3.6 miles\,
  750 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 2) Sat 10/03 – Vist
 a Trail loop\, 3.4 miles\, 830 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Bar
 n\\] 3) Sat 10/10 – Hillside to Neptune table + Meadow\, 4.4 
 miles\, 970 ft elevation \\[meet @ White Barn\\] 4) Sat 10/17 
 – Goodspeed to Nattkemper bench\, 3.8 miles\, 1\,240 ft elevati
 on \\[meet @ Goodspeed lot\\] 5) Sat 10/24 – Hillside + Vista
  Trail loop\, 3.6 miles\, 1\,070 ft elevation \\[meet @ White B
 arn\\] 6) Sat 10/31 – False Lake Meadow & Lake Ilsanjo loop i
 n Trionne-Annadel SP\, 6.1 miles\, 670 ft elevation \\[meet @ An
 nadel's Cobblestone Trailhead\\] 7) Sat 11/07 – Fern Lake + Orc
 hard loop in SDC/Jack London SHP\, 5.5 miles\, 1\,460 ft elevati
 on \\[meet @ Walnut & North St inside SDC\; park on Grove St\\
 ] 8) Sat 11/14 – Bald Mtn summit (w/optional Headwaters detour\
 , 5.8 miles)\, 5.1 miles\, 1\,670 ft elevation \\[meet @ White 
 Barn\\]\n\nPlease note these routes are subject to change based o
 n the group and weather\, as the group does hike in light rain
 s. Wear appropriate footwear for rocky or slippery trails\, and 
 layers. Bring water\, and if desired\, a snack. The group will 
 be limited to 35 participants. \n\nThe hiking series costs $80 (
 plus a $10 parking fee per visit. Note that the Sugarloaf Annua
 l Pass is $59 and valid at Sugarloaf and Jack London SHP)\, or
  free-of-cost for participants with a September 2026 or newer Pa
 rk Rx from a Sonoma County Medical Provider.
