BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sundays in Sonoma at Viansa Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T000000
UID:260624MKGvCqJi7kyVNJpLgLAySA
DESCRIPTION:Viansa Winery feels made for live music\, perched atop the Sum
 mit of Sonoma with sweeping vineyard views and Tuscan-inspired charm. This
  summer and fall\, acclaimed singer-songwriter Greg Lamboy brings his warm
 \, intimate sound to the hilltop terrace for select afternoon performances
  as part of Viansa's outdoor music series. An award-winning guitarist and 
 frontman of the Americana band Pacific Standard\, Lamboy is known for pitc
 h-perfect melodies and deeply personal lyrics. His relaxed\, soulful style
  pairs effortlessly with Viansa's panoramic setting\, estate wines\, and l
 aid-back elegance. Settle in with a tasting\, take in the views\, and enjo
 y an afternoon where strong vocals\, masterful guitar\, and unforgettable 
 songs rise above the everyday. Performance Dates: June 14\, June 21\, July
  12\, July 19\, July 26\, October 4\, and October 18 from 12 pm -3 pm.
LOCATION:Viansa Winery
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/sundays-in-sonoma-at-viansa-winery/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T000000
UID:2603316UvE-3ka50CqwdgLb2IXLA
DESCRIPTION:S.R. Laws: An inspiring Storyteller in Song\n\n        S.R. La
 ws is a performing and recording original musical artist whose work resona
 tes with a familiar warmth while introducing entirely fresh ideas. Hailed 
 by guitarist/promoter Scotty O’Neill as “an ORIGINAL songwriter who kn
 ows how to tell a story clearly in song\,” Laws has built a reputation f
 or songs that capture both nostalgia and innovation.\n\nEarly Influences a
 nd Musical Roots  \n\nGrowing up in Northern California\, Laws developed a
  deep bond with music at an early age. His father worked as a trash collec
 tor\, and young Scott Ray Laws \\(a.k.a. S.R. Laws\\) spent countless hour
 s digging through discarded 45-rpm records. Each discovery—whether caked
  in grime or found pristine—felt like unearthing treasure. The thrill of
  dropping the needle on something new ignited his lifelong passion for son
 g-craft.\n\nThe Texas Pilgrimage  \n\nWith only two suitcases and $500 to 
 his name\, Laws set out for Austin\, Texas—the “Live Music Capital of 
 the World.” There\, open‐mic nights and songwriter showcases became hi
 s classroom. Night after night\, he honed his craft\, forging connections 
 and absorbing the essence of Americana\, roots rock\, and modern folk.\n\n
  “It was such a treat catching your set last night—really refreshing t
 o hear something new and original. Thanks for pulling up a chair and hangi
 ng out with us—we really enjoyed the conversation and the stories behind
  your songs.” - Tripp B.\, Singer-Songwriter\n\nInfluences That Shaped H
 is Voice  \n\nLaws draws inspiration from master storytellers who paved th
 e way for heartfelt\, lyrical music. Artists who have left an indelible ma
 rk on his craft include:\n\n- John Hiatt  \n\n- Lucinda Williams  \n\n- Ro
 dney Crowell  \n\n- Neil Finn  \n\n- Patty Griffin  \n\n- Steve Earle  \n\
 n- Ron Sexsmith  \n\nTheir mastery of narrative and melody has shaped his 
 own artistic journey\, resulting in songs that feel both comfortingly fami
 liar and entirely “out there.”\n\nCritical Acclaim  \n\nColleagues and
  venue owners alike have praised his work and stage presence:  \n\n“Scot
 t Ray Laws is a unique and really cool songwriter…he digs into materials
 \, tells a story in his songs\, and has a clean baritone vocality that is 
 easy on the ears. We had a chance to meet and hang with Scott back in May
 …and I had to have him back for a Wednesday evening.” - Luigi\, Owner 
 of The Listening Room\n\n“Expect slow-burning passion and vivid music…
 the kind of energy that turns into ‘let’s stay for just one more!” -
  Doug\, Owner/Wine Maker at Spicy Vines\n\nCurrent Projects  \n\nNow based
  in Sonoma County\, California\, Laws works tirelessly as a recording\, wr
 iting & touring artist. Through over 100 gig dates a year\, intimate club 
 shows\, festival stages\, house concerts and late-night songwriter circles
 \, he invites audiences to join him on a musical journey—one heartfelt s
 tory at a time.\n\nWith a blend of classic influence\, modern vision\, and
  a voice that feels like home\, S.R. Laws continues to carve out his place
  in the American songwriting landscape.
LOCATION:Bloom Carneros
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108157639?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Need a Mic: Open Mic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T140000
UID:260815mll6KY--6EyhjsDn8vgHng
DESCRIPTION:Welcome poets\, writers\, and artists of Vallejo. My name is R
 ay\, and I am your host of I NEED A MIC OPEN MIC.\n\nThis is more than jus
 t a stage — it’s a space. A space where voices rise\, stories breathe\
 , and truth finds its rhythm. \n\nWhether you carry poems in your chest\,
  songs in your spirit\, or stories that have been waiting for the right mo
 ment — this is your invitation.\n\nWe gather not just to perform\, but t
 o connect. To celebrate the raw\, the real\, and the unapologetically huma
 n art of expression. Every voice matters here. Every perspective adds to t
 he pulse of this room.\n\nBut understand — this is a space built on resp
 ect. While we welcome passion\, depth\, and honesty\, we do not tolerate h
 ate\, disrespect\, or harmful rhetoric. Heavy political agendas that divid
 e rather than inspire have no place here. \n\nThis stage is for expressio
 n\, not oppression.\n\nBring your truth. Bring your courage. Bring your ar
 t.\n\nCome share. Come listen. Come feel something.\n\nBecause someone in 
 that room might need exactly what you have to say.\n\nI NEED A MIC — and
  maybe\, so do you.
LOCATION:City Arts Gallery
URL:https://linktr.ee/INeedAMic
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T170000
UID:260430A1iksuvRXUCIT_p20fZw3Q
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room 
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Misalliance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T161500
UID:2610156K12PfcRqE-DmvgA1SwA_Q
DESCRIPTION:Misalliance is one of George Bernard Shaw’s most spirited an
 d surprising comedies. Set in the drawing room of a prosperous English fam
 ily on a seemingly ordinary afternoon\, the tranquility is shattered when 
 an airplane literally crashes into their greenhouse\, introducing a bold\,
  unconventional aviatrix into the midst of polite society. As suitors circ
 le\, secrets surface\, and romantic expectations unravel\, Shaw turns the 
 traditional courtship comedy on its head with sharp wit and deliciously ta
 ngled misunderstandings.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1386143437005228/1386143493671889/?act
 ive_tab=about
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
