BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Joseph Hooker: Sonoma Valley’s Soldier\, Gambler & Farmer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T203000
UID:261009K3E7fubHgE-zs_O35JONWw
DESCRIPTION:Joseph Hooker is remembered in history as a complex and highly
  controversial military figure. Understanding his past helps explain his f
 uture and his decisions. Before gaining national fame as the commander of 
 the Union's famous Army of the Potomac\, he faced both professional and pe
 rsonal struggles in Sonoma Valley\, many of which he caused himself. Durin
 g his time in Sonoma\, his well-known ego\, brashness\, and questionable d
 ealings led to a series of costly mistakes that would follow him into the 
 Civil War.\n\nJoin us for a fascinating presentation by author Travis P. W
 agner. He will share new information on "Fighting Joe" Hooker's turbulent 
 years in Sonoma Valley. His talk will explore the complex man behind the m
 yth. It will cover his time as a military officer\, a high-stakes gambler\
 , and a struggling frontier farmer\, before he achieved fame in the Civil 
 War.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center - Andrews Hall
URL:https://sonomavalleyhistory.org/event/joseph-hooker-sonoma-valleys-sol
 dier-gambler-farmer/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Healthy Hearty Meal Prep with Erin Shallat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T120000
UID:261005AtTgzz3ljEWBOPf13LOn5A
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, October 5\, 2026 10:00 am to 12:00 pm\n\nWeekly on Mo
 ndays\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCulinary Art
 s\, Wellness\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\n
 Registration Cost:\n\n$25\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registrat
 ion Cost:\n\n$25\n\nAs the founder of Erin Shallat Catering in San Francis
 co\, Erin brings over two decades of experience in transforming nutrition 
 into an art form. Her unique approach intertwines advanced studies in nutr
 ition with a deep passion for the culinary arts. Erin’s goal is to make 
 meal prep approachable and not intimidating for everyone\, encouraging stu
 dents to gain confidence in the kitchen. She believes in working with seas
 onal produce and what’s available\, helping students learn to create hea
 lth-conscious yet tantalizing menus that embrace both flavor and wellness.
  Introducing our Fall/Winter Cooking Series—designed for both returning 
 and new students. This six-week program runs Mondays and Wednesdays\, each
  with a unique focus to offer variety\, skill-building\, and fun throughou
 t the season.Every Monday\, students will dive into healthy\, hearty meal 
 prep sessions. Each class focuses on creating nutritious\, satisfying dish
 es that can be portioned out and taken home—perfect for fueling the week
  ahead. These hands-on sessions ensure participants leave with ready-to-ea
 t meals and new confidence in their culinary skills.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/healthy-hearty-meal-prep-wi
 th-erin-shallat/2026-10-05/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Isis Howard: Monarch Conservation & the Power of Community Science
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T203000
UID:261003O5h54DSgMU6jAv2V_b6jjA
DESCRIPTION:Monarch Conservation & the Power of Community Science\n\nIsis 
 Howard\, Conservation Biologist\, The Xerces Society for Invertebrate Cons
 ervation\n\nWant to help the monarch butterfly? Join us and the Xerces Soc
 iety for an inspiring science talk on the western monarch population. Lear
 n about these butterflies' incredible migration to our California coastlin
 e\, their fragile ecology\, and the simple steps we can all take to help t
 hem recover. While actions are urgent\, the opportunities for impact are g
 reat. You'll leave with fun facts\, local community connections\, and a cl
 ear vision of your role in the monarch's comeback story.\n\nBased in Sonom
 a County\, California\, Isis works to protect western monarch butterflies 
 across their breeding\, migratory\, and overwintering ranges. She provides
  technical assistance and training to land managers and the public on habi
 tat restoration\, monitoring and data collection\, and pollinator conserva
 tion. She also manages community science programs\, including the Western 
 Monarch Count and Western Monarch Milkweed Mapper\, and coordinates the In
 ternational Monarch Monitoring Blitz with several national partners. Isis 
 is an experienced outdoor educator and holds a bachelor of science degree 
 in environmental management and protection from Cal Poly\, San Luis Obispo
LOCATION:First United Methodist Church
URL:https://www.madroneaudubon.org/speakers
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T170000
UID:260930Vj7qkoHh_EaoHXmjBT_JUQ
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two ofrendas in the House of Happy Walls Museum from Oc
 t. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tradi
 tion that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spani
 sh for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the memor
 y of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and adve
 nturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected to 
 the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, traditi
 onal elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, th
 e installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing and 
 travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, and 
 the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared\,
  participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\, 
 and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\, 
 drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a be
 loved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more peop
 le participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitors 
 who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or e
 ven a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
