BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Event: Before Tomorrow by Deb Hazlett
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T180000
UID:261014Pf4_aj34D02rFWuhRXbvZQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event with Deb Hazlett\, author of Befor
 e Tomorrow. This event is free\, but we appreciate your RSVP below so we c
 an plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BOOK She didn't set out to reinvent
  herself. Not at sixty-five. She simply reached a point where staying stil
 l no longer felt like living. After years of quietly wondering if life was
  meant to feel larger than this\, Deb Hazlett sold most of what she owned\
 , taught herself to tow an Airstream travel trailer\, and set out alone to
 ward a future she could neither fully explain nor predict. Before Tomorrow
  is not a travel memoir in the traditional sense. It is the story of a wom
 an learning—late in life and often the hard way—to trust herself beyon
 d the expectations that had shaped her for decades. Alongside the miles tr
 aveled are the quieter\, less glamorous realities of preparing for such a 
 life alone: downsizing\, finances\, fear\, uncertainty\, and the countless
  practical decisions that slowly transformed an impossible idea into reali
 ty. Through mechanical failures\, mountain passes\, storms\, solitude\, un
 expected friendships\, and moments of startling beauty\, the road slowly b
 ecomes something more than movement. It becomes a reckoning with fear\, in
 dependence\, aging\, and the quiet realization that freedom is lived\, one
  mile at a time. Reflective\, honest\, and quietly humorous\, Before Tomor
 row speaks to anyone who has ever wondered whether it is too late to begin
  living more fully. "Before Tomorrow is part travel memoir\, part practica
 l guide\, and entirely inspiring. Her story is proof that adventure doesn'
 t have an age limit—it only requires the courage to begin." — Scott St
 illman\, author of I Don't Want to Grow Up "Exceptionally well written..."
  — Midwest Book Review "Loved it!" — Reedsy Discovery ABOUT THE AUTHOR
  Deb Hazlett is the author of Before Tomorrow\, a memoir about choosing yo
 ur own path at age sixty-five. After a near-death experience\, she sold mo
 st of what she owned\, learned to tow an Airstream travel trailer\, and se
 t out alone across the country. What began as a cross-country adventure be
 came a journey toward trusting her own voice and discovering it is never t
 oo late to begin again. A native Northern Californian with deep roots in N
 apa\, Deb continues to write about courage\, self-discovery\, and the quie
 t confidence that comes from finally trusting your own voice.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1449732177063448/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
