BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ocean's Unseen Frequencies by Firuze Gokce - Art Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T190000
UID:261014hB7zJP7E-0uDc1dubllPOA
DESCRIPTION:I’m delighted to invite you to “Ocean’s Unseen Frequenci
 es\,” my new art exhibition celebrating the hidden soundscapes of the oc
 ean and the fascinating world of whale communication.\n\nThrough my artwor
 k\, I transform real whale sound spectrograms\, acoustic patterns\, and sc
 ientific observations into vibrant visual expressions. My work explores th
 e connections between sound\, science\, art\, and the natural world\, invi
 ting us to experience the ocean in a different way and discover the extrao
 rdinary stories hidden beneath the surface.\n\nThe event will also feature
  a special talk by Michael Stocker\, acoustician\, naturalist\, musician\,
  and founding director of Ocean Conservation Research. With decades of exp
 erience in marine bioacoustics and ocean conservation\, Michael has dedica
 ted his work to understanding how underwater noise affects marine life. I
 ’m excited to bring together art and scientific perspectives for an enga
 ging conversation about ocean sound and the importance of protecting the a
 coustic environment of marine animals.\n\nThis exhibition is especially me
 aningful to me as I prepare for the next chapter of my artistic journey. I
 ’ve been selected to participate in an Arctic Circle Art Residency in Sv
 albard\, where I hope to explore the soundscapes of the Arctic\, from whal
 e vocalizations to the cracking and shifting of sea ice\, and translate th
 ese sounds into new works of art.\n\nI’ll also be fundraising at this ev
 ent to help support my Arctic Circle Art Residency. Your presence\, encour
 agement\, and support will help me bring this project to life and continue
  exploring the intersection of art\, science\, and ocean conservation.\n\n
 I would love to see you there\, share the stories behind my paintings\, he
 ar Michael’s insights\, and celebrate the incredible world of sound that
  connects us to our planet.\n\nThank you for being part of this journey. I
  look forward to seeing you!
LOCATION:Keller Street Co-work
URL:https://orangeorca.art/events/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
