UID:2610125qbGgEHgL0K2J0Bj8FehGA
DESCRIPTION:4TH Annual American Roots Mini-Fest Downtown Sonoma - 3 bands 
 in The Alley at Murphys\, Sat\, Oct 24 2:30-9:30\, Outdoors\, all day... H
 attie Craven\, Back pOrchEstra and The Wild Premonitions.\n\n"Something Ne
 w and Something Familiar"... Roots Rock\, Americana\, Country Blues\, West
 ern Swing\, Cajun\, and New Orleans music...\n\nno cover\, Tip the perform
 ers! $10\\+ donation suggested\n\nHattie Craven 2:30-4:00\n\nHattie Craven
  has lived and breathed music since her early years with her father\, awar
 d-winning performer Joe Craven. Hattie draws musical influences from Amy W
 inehouse\, Joni Mitchell\, James Brown\, Louis Prima\, and so many more. S
 he effectively reimagines traditional folk\, bluegrass\, country\, jazz an
 d pop\,\n\ncreating new music that is truly her own. Hattie is also a fine
  writer of original songs that explore themes of love\, loss and resilienc
 e. https://www.hattiecraven.com\n\nBack pOrchEstra: 4:45-6:45\n\nSemi-Acou
 stic Original Indie Rock & the American Roots\n\nthat inspired it: Country
  Blues\, Cajun\, Roots Rock\,\n\nAmericana\, Singer/Songwriter music with 
 rich tones:\n\nCandy Girard\, Tim Eschliman\, Mark Larson\, Jen Rund\, Lui
 s Rodriguez... originals and reworked classics by Hank Williams\, Taj Maha
 l\, Dan Hicks\, NRBQ\, JJ Cale\, Big Al Amderson\, Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob 
 Wills\, Jimmy Reed\, Joseph & Cleome Falcon... recent single: https://orcd
 .co/7jjvmmx ... "What Does Your Heart Say?" - a Breezy west coast rock\, a
  hopeful idealistic Americana love song duet\, celebrating the new "Storie
 s In The Heart" album\, listen now!: https://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\nhttps://ww
 w.BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nThe Wild Premonitions: 7:30-9:30\n\nA never-before
  summit of players... an experiment of many genres: Rock\, Blues\, Jazz\, 
 Funk\, Zydeco... Mike Rinta\, Tim Eschliman\, Roy Blumenfeld\, Kevin Zuffi
  and Ian Lamson... players from The Blues Project\, Rhythmtown-Jive\, Loui
 siana Time Travelers\, Sly Stone\, Commander Cody & His Western Airmen.\n\
 n464 1st St E\, Sonoma\, CA 95476 \\(707\\) 935-0660\n\nSongs from all ove
 r the map!...\n\nsee also\n\nRoy Blumenfeld: https://bluesproject.net/bios
 /\n\nhttp://www.rhythmtown-jive.com\n\nhttps://www.mikerintamusic.com\n\nh
 ttps://timeschliman.com/LouisianaTimeTravelers.html\n\nCommander Cody & Hi
 s Western Airmen YouTube Playlist: https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLSGI
 mH0Ow80I&si=ib9D\\_7PpEiKJ2rFn\n\nPreview the music:\n\nThe Blues Project\
 , Hattie Craven\, Back pOrchEstra \, Roy Blumenfeld\, Rhythmtown-Jive\, Mi
 ke Rinta -\n\n4TH Annual American Roots Mini-Fest Playlists:\n\n... on you
 Tube:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLEi6QQx2MsMM\n\n...on Spot
 ify:\n\nhttps://open.spotify.com/playlist/17CVSLarIOMxTN03uhfFTA?si=F-\\_4
