SUMMARY:Blind Scream Haunted House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T220000
UID:2609216lVYpuOkMUO5OqC9EIUgXQ
DESCRIPTION:Open 13 nights only\, join the Doc and his family and step int
 o over 20\,000 square feet of haunted horror in the heart of Santa Rosa. T
 his year we have 2 distinct haunts for you to sink your teeth into.\n\nBli
 nd Scream Haunted House features the all new Caverns of Carnage where wind
 ing tunnels\, claustrophobic chambers\, and forgotten caverns have danger 
 lurking around every corner. The deeper you go\, the harder it becomes to 
 tell what’s part of the cave and what’s watching you from within it.\n
 \nBLACKOUT Haunted House is a pitch-black maze. All you have to guide your
  way is one glow stick… and the creatures stalking your every step. Ever
 y sense will be tested. Every turn is a challenge. And one wrong move… t
 he scream is yours.\n\nFeed your terrors today and get your tickets before
  it's too late. Once the 13 nights are gone\, the haunt disappears until n
 ext year!\n\nLocation - 98 Santa Rosa Plaza\, Downtown Santa Rosa \\(at th
 e corners of 1st Street and A Street\\). South of the Santa Rosa Plaza par
 king garage.
LOCATION:Blind Scream Haunted House
URL:https://www.blindscream.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adrian West Band
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
UID:2609211HnixvFkpUya-zmop3hP7A
DESCRIPTION:The six-piece Adrian West Band will perform from 3 - 5pm with 
 an intermission in the Atrium room of the Osher JCC. Will include Joe Esco
 bar on the Grand Piano. Ticketed show. Details coming soon.\n\nAdrian West
  Band is a six-piece acoustic rock ensemble from Oakland. They play a fun 
 mix of originals\, covers and instrumentals plus some popular Jazz standar
 ds. Some describe their sound as “Paul Simon meets Talking Heads”.\n\n
 A native of Montreal\, Adrian enjoys setting philosophical lyrics to uplif
 ting music. Whether telling a story about a skinny-dipping episode gone aw
 ry or grappling with the many challenges facing humanity\, his lyrics are 
 fueled by equal parts hope\, realism and whimsy and ride atop a steady wav
 e of catchy music.\n\nCovers and standards the band will play will include
  some or all of these: Ants Marching (Dave Matthews) Brass In Pocket (The 
 Pretenders) Closer to Fine (Indigo Girls) Feels So Good (Chuck Mangione) A
 rmando’s Rhumba (Chick Corea) Happy People (Kenny Garrett) Linus & Lucy 
 (Vince Guaraldi)\n\nInstrumentation: 2 vocalists\, acoustic guitar\, elec.
  violin\, piano\, upright bass\, alto sax\, drums\, percussion\, live loop
 ing\n\nAdrian West - vocals\, acoustic guitar\, elec. violin & live loopin
 g Joseph Escobar on piano Amy Obenski - vocals\, percussion Chris Haag - a
 lto sax Aaron Germain - upright bass Dan Foltz - drums\n\nFor more informa
 tion\, visit www.adrianwest.com
LOCATION:Osher Marin JCC
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/adrian-west-band/199644
 71/2026-10-25T15
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Clay + Bloom: Ceramics\, Floral Design and Watercolor Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T140000
UID:260920Va8hVI3PuUCNBvqoP5kwfg
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to this multimedia workshop. Two of our seasoned instr
 uctors are teaming up to bring you an extra special collaboration.\n\nIn t
 his event You’ll create a vase for your favorite floral arrangement any 
 time of year\, plus once this piece you’ve created has been fired we’l
 l all reconvene and create both a special floral arrangement specifically 
 for this event and we’ll learn how to paint a watercolor still life comb
 ing all of these elements into a truly unique piece of Art!\n\nThis worksh
 op meets twice\, our first meeting is Sunday October 4th 10am - 2pm where 
 we host you for our clay play and Sunday October 25th 10am - 2pm for our F
 loral arranging and Watercolor Still Life painting \n\nWe’ll cover Cera
 mic Slab Building techniques for our vases\, floral arranging and basic Wa
 tercolor techniques for our still life. \n\nWe supply: \n\nClay\, Slab T
 emplates\, Ceramic Tools\, We’ll provide the Glaze and Glazing once your
  vases have been bisque fired\, all flowers needed for arranging at the 2n
 d meeting of this workshop\, Frog/Floral Structural Mechanics/Floral Tape 
 for arrangements\, watercolors for use day of\, Palettes\, Brushes\, Cups 
 and Paper. \n\nYou will walk away from the workshop with a ceramic vase\,
  a beautiful floral arrangement and a watercolor still life that you yours
 elf have fully created! \n\nLunch provided for a small donation\, \\[plea
 se indicate dietary preferences beforehand if possible\\].
LOCATION:Kickwheel Sonoma
URL:https://kickwheelsonoma.com/products/clay-and-bloom-workshop-with-dean
 na-and-gena-sunday-october-4th
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Los Colores de Otoño (Colors of Autumn)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
UID:260918KiEihAMuZEmSkggZovauUA
DESCRIPTION:Los Colores de Otoño \\(The Colors of Autumn\\) is a communit
 y day in Spanish for the whole family to enjoy nature\, art\, culture\, an
 d the season together.\n\nCome in costume and spend the day surrounded by 
 papel picado\, Mexican food\, art and crafts inspired by Halloween and Dí
 a de los Muertos\, and opportunities to get an up-close look at the region
 ’s wildlife. There will be activities for kids and adults\, community or
 ganizations sharing resources\, and a collection of animal skulls and pelt
 s to explore. And everyone who comes in costume gets candy!\n\nWhether wit
 h family\, friends\, a partner\, or on your own\, this will be a day to co
 nnect\, create\, and celebrate the colors and traditions that make this ti
 me of year so special.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/coloresynaturaleza/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nell & Jim & Kalei Trio LIVE at The Lost Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T183000
UID:260917F9WpX5c8-UaHePQdDdkCdg
DESCRIPTION:Live and Local in Northern California! Nell & Jim & Kalei
  Trio present Songs & Stories of Migration\, Home\, Mystery & Love. Think
  Bluegrass  meets Singer/Songwriter meets Folk meets Country. Take a musi
 cal journey through themes of migration\, home\, mystery and love - in ter
 ritory both familiar and surprising\, reflective and joyful. Featuring ori
 ginal music and beloved covers\, beautiful vocal harmonies and hot pickin
 ’. Guitar\, Banjo\, Accordion\, Flute.\n\nABOUT THE ARTISTS : Nell Robin
 son is hailed as “one of the freshest voices in roots music” and a mod
 ern-day Patsy Cline. Her acclaimed album “The Rose of No-Man’s Land”
  became a PBS special\, and she’s performed at major festivals and on A 
 Prairie Home Companion\, captivating audiences with her heartfelt original
  songs and vibrant takes on tradition.\n\nJim Nunally is a Grammy-winning 
 guitarist and vocalist renowned for his powerful bluegrass style and deep 
 musical roots. A longtime member of the David Grisman Bluegrass Experience
 \, his original songs and virtuosic playing have earned him acclaim across
  the roots music community.\n\nKalei Yamanoha is a versatile multi-instrum
 entalist and composer known for his dynamic performances across Hawaiʻi a
 nd the mainland. He has led bands for Flynn Creek Circus and The Traveling
  Spectacular\, and brings a unique blend of folk\, Americana\, and circus 
 music to every stage. A master of accordion\, steel guitar\, and more\, hi
 s artistry fuses Hawaiian\, folk\, Americana\, and circus music\, creating
  an engaging and original sound.
LOCATION:The Lost Church Santa Rosa
URL:https://www.nellandjim.com/tour-data/2026/lost-church-santa-rosa-octob
 er-25
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Aspirations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T180000
UID:260916qiDgyn4zXEWTZsXZSghp8A
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  9/15/26\n\n**OCTOBER EXHIBIT: AS
 PIRATIONS**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– September 28 – October 25\, 2026**\n\
 n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, October 3\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Laura 
 Roney and Linda Loveland Reid and learn about their art and inspiration. 
  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Laura Roney\,** unveils **Aspirations**\, a new collect
 ion of paintings in oil\, celebrating the unique differing goals people se
 t during our lives\, challenging us to take bold steps forward.  Of unive
 rsal inspiration**\, Aspiration and Awe** splashes the Milky Way’s starr
 y brilliance across the heavens\, capturing our imagination and hope as wo
 rldly cares are left behind.  Moving from natural forces to human endeavo
 r\, looking toward social change\, **Aspiring to Vote**\, the portrait of 
 a hopeful suffragette\, evokes the dream for a better future.  A lifetime
  goal for many\, the marathon\, **Aspiring for 26.2\,** captures the early
  morning excitement waiting for start times.  “People doing ordinary th
 ings but dreaming larger for the future has been a great inspiration for t
 his series.  I hope folks will be inspired by the boldness of people’s 
 dreams\,” commented Roney on her inspiration for the work.\n\nArt has be
 en a lifelong passion for Roney.  Beginning her art studies at a young ag
 e\, whatever avenue she was pursuing in life\, she continued her artistic 
 endeavors.  After a successful career in microbiology and pharmaceutical 
 research\, a family move to Northern California enabled Roney to focus on 
 her art.  She received her MFA from Academy of Art University\, San Franc
 isco.\n\nMeet the artist: Roney will host the Gallery on September 30 and 
 October 1 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features 
 Linda Loveland Reid’s **Intentional Chaos\,** a collection of exciting m
 ixed-media works that explode with excitement and energy. Random patterns\
 , amorphous shapes and dancing dribbles magically coalesce into bold state
 ments.  Intriguing and compelling\, like interlocking gears\, in **Patter
 ns of Memory** multiple patterns interlock on fields of gold and black.  
 “I love throwing ink\, paint and even coffee onto a blank canvas and cre
 ating through instinct\, gesture and emotion.  Distilling energy into sma
 ller works brings new challenges and some happy surprises\,” noted Reid 
 on her creative process.\n\nMeet the artist: Reid will host the Gallery on
  October 23 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\n Also join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG
 **\, Thursday\, October 1\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1
 st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and crea
 tivity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nU
 pstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431
 -4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \
 n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvd
 rio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zach Neil
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T130000
UID:260910F6oXleYhfUGGVYNQYcp1TA
DESCRIPTION:Updated Bio\n\nZach Neil is the 2022 Texas Country Music Assoc
 iation’s Male Artist of the Year and has earned five consecutive Top 40 
 Texas country singles – not bad for a guy who planned to follow in his d
 ad’s footsteps and become a farmer. Farming was the family business and 
 still is\, but Zach decided to use the work ethic he acquired from his fam
 ily and focus on a career in music. Zach is a singer\, songwriter and live
  performer who uniquely puts his own twist on traditional country music. \
 n\n“I love playing live. Every show is different\, every crowd is differ
 ent. Each night on stage is a chance for me to grow and share my love for 
 country music.”\n\nHis Texas country hits include:\n\n•	“When She Dr
 inks Whiskey” \\(2019\\)\n\n•	“Something In The Stars” \\(2020\\)\
 n\n•	“Half Bad” \\(2021\\)\n\n•	“Long Live The Cowboy” \\(2022
 \\)\n\n•	“All The Pretty Horses\,” \\(2022\\) – which stayed in th
 e Top 20 of the Texas Country Music Chart for multiple weeks. \n\nZach’s
  new single “Till The Numbers Run Out” is now on Texas country radio\,
  on all streaming platforms\, and available for download wherever you get 
 your music.\n\nVisit www.zachneilmusic.com to learn more about Zach and fo
 r a complete list of upcoming tour dates.
LOCATION:O'Brien Estate Winery
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108708002?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
