BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Charlie Ginsburgh to present at the Napa Valley Photographic Socie
 ty
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261026T203000
UID:261014xBjBwEtupES2-SDnioHJ5Q
DESCRIPTION:Please join fellow photography enthusiasts for Charlie Ginsbur
 gh’s presentation on what makes a good photography image.\n\nCharlie Gin
 sburgh has been involved in photography since 2011. In reflecting on his p
 ersonal photographic style\, Charlie states\, “I find that I am attracte
 d to the idea of ‘making the commonplace\, uncommon’ in the world arou
 nd me and especially in nature. I can be in a group of people overlooking 
 a truly magnificent panoramic vista\, and darn if I am not most interested
  in the little weedy flower-thing nearly buried in the dust at my feet.”
  \n\nCharlie has been involved in offering image commentary for the last 
 seven years\, offering commentary to over 250 SF Bay Area camera club and 
 PSA affiliated clubs events.\n\nHe is currently both a Northern California
  Council of Camera Clubs \\(N4C\\) and Photographic Society of America \\(
 PSA\\) Photography judge and has participated in photographic competitions
  domestically throughout the Chicago / San Francisco Bay areas and interna
 tionally for PSA. Charlie has also been a speaker at the last four N4C Fot
 oclave conferences. He has also provided programs for local camera clubs o
 n Action Photography\, Macro Photography\, Flower Photography\, and Compos
 iting / Photoshop editing. Charlie is currently the N4C Judges Chair\, a p
 ast President of the Peninsula Camera Club in San Mateo\, CA\, and is an N
 4C Fellow.  Charlie will critique member-submitted photos after his prese
 ntation. \n\nExamples of his photography are provided on his web site \\(
 https://charlie-g.smugmug.com\\) and he can be reached via E-mail at cgins
 burgh@gmail.com\n\nNapa Valley Photographic Society \\(NVPS\\) promotes th
 e art and science of photography\, providing education\, image appreciatio
 n\, inspiration\, and exchange of technologies. Most months\, we invite gu
 est speakers to evaluate our images.  Guests are welcome to attend.  Che
 ck the website for more information: http://www.napavalleyphotographicsoci
 ety.org.
LOCATION:Napa Senior Center
URL:http://napavalleyphotographicsociety.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
