BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Skunk Funk Samhain Suarez
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T190000
UID:260910k8L-Gb43p0qbEjhuOgCKAg
DESCRIPTION:Funky\, Punky and Intergalactic: Skunk Funk traveled from the 
 dystopian planet of Esoterra only to crash land onto a small suburb in Ame
 rican Canyon\, CA. In orbit or on Earth\, it is their sole mission to brin
 g every crowd they woo an animated yet uplifting and off the wall experien
 ce. A spellbinding fusion of Punk/Funk/Ska is their medium of choice in th
 eir battle against degradation and lameness.\n\n \n\nThere is 4 distinct p
 ieces to this blue print\, it didn't happen by accident. Tides were shifte
 d and stars rearranged to unite these 4 cosmic misfits:\n\n \n\nBobby "Bob
 o the Sequel" Roses - Lead Vocals/Bass\n\nMax "Billion Powers" Gee - Vocal
 s/Guitar\n\nBryan "Cuban-B" Rose's - Vocals\n\nNick "Lt. Whitty" Whitmire 
 - Drums/Vocals\n\n \n\nPresently\, the four manifest a sound so distinctiv
 e and high energy\; they are a hot commodity anywhere they go. Over the co
 urse of the last 4 years\, they have managed to independently release an E
 P entitled “Too Fresh to Function” and a full-length album entitled 
 “Possession 4 Sale”. Most recently\, they have released they're best w
 ork yet through their 2018 "Cirque Du Skank" EP\, which also comes with mu
 sic video. Their new full-length album\, "Skunk Soup"\, has been served up
  1/23/2021. They plan on recording and performing live in 2022.\n\n \n\nSk
 unk Funk’s diverse sound and energetic live shows has earned them chance
 s to perform at numerous venues including:\n\nThe Uptown Theatre \\(Napa\\
 )\n\n924 Gilman \\(Berkeley\\)\n\nGolden Bull \\(Oakland\\)\n\nCow Palace 
 \\(SF\\)\n\nBrick & Mortar Music Hall \\(SF\\)\n\nMilk Bar \\(SF\\)\n\nNec
 k of the Woods \\(SF\\)\n\nDNA Lounge \\(SF\\)\n\nEl Rio \\(SF\\)\n\nThe N
 OS Event Center \\(San Bernardino\\)\n\nHoly Diver \\(Sacramento\\)\n\nNap
 a Smith Brewery \\(Vallejo\\)\n\nBlue Note \\(Napa\\)\n\nBurnt Ramen \\(Ri
 chmond\\)\n\nStag’s Leap Winery \\(Napa\\)\n\n​\n\nThey’ve also had 
 the pleasure to play numerous festivals such as Bottle Rock Napa Valley\, 
 Chalice Festival\, Hemp Con\, Heart and Soulstice Festival\, Reggae in the
  Trees \\(OR\\)\, Sacramento Hemp Fest\, Napa Porchfest and more.\n\n \n\n
 In their travels they have shared the stage with many different acts inclu
 ding The Black Keys\, Zac Brown Band\, Primus\, Violent Femmes\, Joan Jett
 \, Cake\, Rodrigo y Gabriela\, Train\, Michael Franti\, Bad Religion\, The
  Black Crowes\, The Flaming Lips\, The Aggrolites\, RBL Posse\, Indubious\
 , Bumpin' Uglies\, Mystic Roots\, Prezident Brown\, Marlon Asher\, Baby Ba
 sh\, Paul Wall\, Fortunate Youth\, Yukmouth\, B-Legit and many more to com
 e in the near future.\n\nWith dynamism and music like theirs\, your party\
 , show\, event\, wedding\, concert\, anything is sure to be a hit and full
  of the most rockin'\, high energy and groovy tunes. For more information 
 on booking and contacts please be sure to check the links below.\n\n \n\nW
 ebsite: https://www.skunkfunkofficial.com\n\nBooking & Contact: Skunkfunk7
 07@gmail.com\n\nSpotify: https://open.spotify.com/artist/0xMpoSyMlZuxPWuTe
 2fyOY?nd=1\n\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/skunkfunkmusic\n\nTwitter
 : @skunkfunk707\n\nInstagram: @skunkfunkmusic\n\nSound Cloud: https://www.
 soundcloud.com/skunk-funk\n\nYouTube Channel: SkunkFunkVision
LOCATION:4th Corner Speakeasy
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108636042?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
