BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Lyft and Cab Rides by Wells Call Injury Lawyers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T100000
UID:2610124TFzA3HFmUK3ZduKCGCdAw
DESCRIPTION:According to the Annual Report of California DUI Management In
 formation System\, of the total number of crash fatalities in 2018\, 32.1%
  were alcohol-related in California. We are committed to helping our commu
 nity not be a part of this statistic.\n\nWe pride ourselves on making our 
 community safer and giving back to our neighbors as much as we can. That i
 s why this holiday season\, if you decide to go out and celebrate\, we wil
 l pay for your cab ride home to ensure that you make it home safely.\n\nWe
 ’d like to introduce a new community initiative: Free Lyft and Cab Ride 
 Program to help reduce the number of drunk drivers on the road during the 
 holidays. This holiday season\, if you decide to go and drink\, please mak
 e the responsible choice to grab a ride home instead of getting behind the
  wheel. We will reimburse you for your fare home\, so save that receipt!\n
 \nRead more about our Holiday Ride-Share Program below for full details. 
 \n\nNote: Because of their track record on failing to protect women from s
 exual assault and their lack of regard for consumer rights\, we do not sup
 port Uber.\n\nHow it Works:\n\nThe program is simple. If you have been dri
 nking – take an Lyft or cab\, and you’ll get a reimbursement from us!\
 n\nWe want you home safe this holiday season.\n\nQualifying Holidays:\n\nS
 uper Bowl Sunday\n\nSt. Patrick’s Day\n\nCinco de Mayo\n\nIndependence D
 ay\n\nLabor Day\n\nHalloween\n\nThanksgiving Eve & Day\n\nNew Year’s Eve
  & Day\n\nDetails to the Program:\n\nRide must be on Lyft or a cab \\(Not 
 Uber\\)\n\nRides must be in Solano County\n\nRides must be taken between 5
  pm on the day of the holiday and 10 am the next morning.\n\nYou must be o
 f legal drinking age to qualify \\(21 and over\\).\n\nValid for one\, one-
 way ride to a safe destination.\n\nLimit one reimbursement per household.\
 n\nA maximum value of $25.00 anywhere within Solano County.\n\nThe maximum
  value includes a tip of up to 10%. Anything above a 10% tip on the base f
 are will not be reimbursed.\n\nParticipation in this promotion is limited 
 to the first 25 submissions.\n\nWhen Will I Get My Reimbursement?\n\nWithi
 n 10 business days\, you must submit a copy of your receipt and photo ID v
 ia mail to our office. We will mail you a check for your reimbursement of 
 a qualifying submission within 30 days of the holiday.\n\nWells Call Injur
 y Lawyers 1455 Oliver Rd \\#110 Fairfield\, CA 94534 707-273-1278 www.well
 scall.com/\n\nSubmissions are limited and will fill up fast\, so don’t d
 elay submitting your reimbursement.
LOCATION:CA 94534
URL:https://www.wellscall.com/free-ride-share/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Day of the Dead with the Herd: Ancestors\, Horses & the Healing of
  Grief
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T153000
UID:2610109Lix2I4VT02NmCOTmMDF8w
DESCRIPTION:Day of the Dead with the Herd: Ancestors\, Horses & the Healin
 g of Grief\n\nJoin Alane Freund\, LMFT\, and the Heart & Mind Equine herd 
 for an intimate daylong retreat honoring our ancestors\, remembering loved
  ones\, and exploring grief and healing. Inspired by Día de los Muertos a
 nd seasonal traditions of remembrance\, this unique experience combines eq
 uine-assisted therapy\, somatic practices\, sound healing\, and ritual. Pa
 rticipants are invited to bring a meaningful object for a communal ancesto
 r altar. No horse experience necessary. Lunch and refreshments included. L
 imited to 15 participants.\n\nSunday\, November 1 | 9:30 AM–3:30 PM Wood
 acre\, CA\n\nRegistration: https://www.heartmindequine.com/day-of-the-dead
LOCATION:Heart and Mind Equine
URL:https://www.heartmindequine.com/day-of-the-dead
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de los Muertos Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T190000
UID:261003Z5KNitBoX0-1MchpUctj2A
DESCRIPTION:Join us on November 1st for a magical\n\nDía de Los Muertos C
 elebration\n\nBring your family and friends as we honor our loved ones and
  immerse ourselves in this beautiful tradition.\n\nSugar Skull Decorating 
 & Themed Art Project Face Painting Traditional Mexican Food & Refreshing D
 rinks Quetzalén Dance Presentation \\(Ballet Folklórico\\)\n\nThis is a 
 family-friendly occasion open to all ages!\n\nEnjoy delicious tamales and 
 a variety of delicious Agua Fresca made by Cielito\, desserts\, and the tr
 aditional Pan de Muerto.\n\nQuetzalén Folklórico begins at 5:00 PM\n\nFe
 stivities will take place inside and on our outdoor patio.
LOCATION:Art Escape Sonoma
URL:https://www.artescapesonoma.com/dia-de-los-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Focaccia + Wine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T140000
UID:261002ZnrS1DWVLE61AhQI0-gLXw
DESCRIPTION:Kinda like brunch\, but better.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed after
 noon of fresh focaccia\, Adruni wine\, vineyard views\, and a little creat
 ivity around the table.\n\nWe’ll welcome you to Adruni Vineyards with a 
 glass of their inaugural sparkling wine release and sweeping views of Dr
 y Creek Valley. From there\, find your seat and settle in—this isn't you
 r traditional cooking class.\n\nBreanna of Riverbend Farm Stand will have 
 the sourdough prepared and ready for you to get straight to the fun part. 
 She’ll show you how to stretch and dimple your dough before you make you
 r way through a beautiful\, seasonal topping bar to create a focaccia enti
 rely your own.\n\nThere’s no long sourdough lesson or pressure to get it
  perfect. Breanna will be alongside you to guide\, answer questions\, and 
 handle the baking while you sip\, create\, and enjoy the afternoon.\n\nOnc
 e the focaccia goes into the oven\, we’ll gather back around the table f
 or a taste of Adruni wines and light accompaniments while everything bakes
 .\n\nAnd you won't leave empty-handed.\n\nYour freshly baked focaccia is y
 ours to take home\, along with a Riverbend Farm Stand sourdough starter an
 d care guide so you can try your hand at it again in your own kitchen.\n\n
 Come with a friend or come on your own. Either way\, we'll save you a seat
  at the table.\n\nSunday\, November 1 Adruni Vineyards | Dry Creek Valley 
 $145 per person Limited to just 12 guests\n\nAdditional Adruni wines will
  be available for purchase during the afternoon.
LOCATION:Adruni Vineyards
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/focaccia-wine-tickets-2002485607357?aff=e
 bdssbdestsearch
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reggae Roadhouse!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T180000
UID:261001N6VMA_v8jEGfUPARESjOvQ
DESCRIPTION:If you are a lover of all styles of Reggae music\, then this i
 s the event for you! Come enjoy a sound system session hosted by the Uncon
 ditional Love Sound DJs and dance to tunes ranging from ‘60s Ska to mode
 rn Steppers! Get ready for 6-hours of heavy rhythms exploring the many sub
 genres of Reggae music (Rock Steady\, Roots\, Dancehall\, Dub\, Lovers Roc
 k\, etc.). Powered by Dr. Wood's Soundsystem—strictly vinyl on the decks
 ! Full bar and kitchen!
LOCATION:Rio Nido Roadhouse
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/reggae-roadhouse-tickets-2002746778527?af
 f=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
