BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Endless Inspiration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T180000
UID:261014EGDas0tYskGyom3neGSxng
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  10/12/26\n\n**NOVEMBER EXHIBIT: 
 ENDLESS INSPIRATION**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES **– October 26  – November 22\
 , 2026**\n\n**RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, November 7\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to
  meet Ron Sumner and Karen Miller and learn about their art and inspiratio
 n.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a 
 beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSo
 noma County artist\, **Ron Sumner\,** presents **Endless Inspiration**\, a
  collection of new paintings and classic works that highlight his lifelong
  love of nature featuring landscapes\, animals and wildlife\, with a speci
 al focus on birds.  The essence of this golden state shines forth in “C
 alifornia Hills\,” a large oil painting of a sweep of oak covered hills.
    Turning to wildlife\, Sumner’s masterful watercolor rendition in th
 e “Young Fox” captures its wild nature on stark alert.  And the compe
 lling presence of a most majestic bird is beautifully memorialized in his 
 “Blue Heron” watercolor.  Other birds depicted in his works include p
 arrots\, penguins and owls.  “In my painting\, I always strive to trans
 late my emotional response to the world of nature around us – to share t
 his deep feeling with those who view my work\,” commented Sumner on his 
 inspiration.\n\nA lifelong Northern Californian\, Sumner began his art tra
 ining in school.  After earning a BFA from the California College of Arts
  & Crafts\, he was a technical illustrator for a number of years before tr
 ansitioning to a full-time fine arts painter.  With an emphasis in waterc
 olor\, he has won numerous awards\, including Best of Show at the Society 
 of Western Artists.  His portrait of John F. Kennedy is part of the perma
 nent collection at the John F. Kennedy Library.  He has exhibited widely 
 and was part of the Veterans Art Show for CA vets in 2023.\n\nMeet the art
 ist: Sumner will co-host Art Nite on 11/5 from 5 pm to 7 pm.\n\nThe Stairw
 ay Smallworks Showcase features **Karen Miller’**s **Historic Gems\,** f
 eaturing pastel paintings that honor our history – local artifacts that 
 are disappearing.  Highlighting this exhibit\, “Ghost Bridge\,” an ea
 rly 20th century railroad bridge known as Healdsburg Railroad Bridge is so
 on to give way for the Smart Train.  Its unique style is a key element to
  our local character but sadly could not be upgraded for modern rail.  Fr
 om old trucks to a beloved schoolhouse\, these paintings harken fond memor
 ies.  Part of our world for years\, they enriched our lives and are not t
 o be forgotten.  Noted Miller on the impetus for her series\, “I want t
 o catch old things before they’re gone – memorializing those things cl
 ose to our hearts.”\n\nMeet the artist: Miller will host the Gallery on 
 October 26 and November 2\, 11\, 14 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n Also j
 oin us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\, November 5\, 5 – 7 pm. 
  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a communi
 ty event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries participati
 ng.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\,
  Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    
 **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beve
 rly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Freestyle Playground Dance Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T193000
UID:261008JXjAvh7fpEa-wngJl_a-vQ
DESCRIPTION:Freestyle Playground — 4-Week Dance & Movement Series\n\nExp
 lore. Play. Create. Express.\n\nReady to discover new ways of moving and e
 xpressing yourself through dance?\n\nFreestyle Playground is a playful\, c
 reative dance class designed to expand your movement vocabulary\, spark yo
 ur imagination\, and help you discover your own unique movement style.\n\n
 Through guided freestyle exercises\, imaginative movement concepts\, music
 ality\, elements of popping\, rhythm\, and body awareness\, you'll explore
  new ways to move\, experiment\, and create.\n\nEach week\, we'll introduc
 e different movement tools and concepts that you can combine\, build upon\
 , and incorporate into your own dancing.\n\nThis isn't a choreography-base
 d class. It's about exploration\, curiosity\, and the freedom to move with
 out worrying about getting it "right."\n\nWhether you're an experienced da
 ncer looking for fresh inspiration or someone curious about exploring move
 ment\, all levels are welcome!\n\nClass Details\n\n📍 Laguna Lab | Sebas
 topol\, CA\n\n📅 4 Tuesdays: October 27\, November 3\, 10 & 17\n\n⏰ 6:
 30–7:30 PM\n\n💃 All levels welcome!\n\nCome expand your creativity\, 
 discover new movement possibilities\, and experience the joy of freestyle 
 dance!\n\nNo perfection. Just movement\, music\, imagination & PLAY!
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://www.tickettailor.com/events/lagunalab/2417443
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T170000
UID:2610043hb_4BZrV0mQX2v4PuwTsw
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Kabbalah of Meaning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T193000
UID:261001dLz5J5usKUy2vjRp4Kmiww
DESCRIPTION:Jewish Wisdom for a Life That Matters\n\nNo matter how much we
  achieve\, something within us still asks: “Is this it? Isn’t there so
 mething more?”\n\nThe Kabbalah of Meaning is a new six-session JLI cours
 e exploring the Jewish answer to that question. What are we really searchi
 ng for—and where can it be found?\n\nDrawing on Kabbalah and centuries o
 f Jewish wisdom\, we’ll uncover the essential building blocks of a deepl
 y meaningful life. We’ll explore how purpose can be found in our work\, 
 relationships\, challenges\, accomplishments\, and even the ordinary routi
 nes that fill our days.\n\nYou don’t have to revamp your life. You don
 ’t need to meditate on a mountaintop. You simply need a new lens through
  which to see the rich world of meaning already woven into every part of y
 our life.\n\nThoughtful\, practical\, and surprisingly relevant\, this cou
 rse offers fresh perspectives and useful tools for living with greater cla
 rity\, connection\, and intention.\n\nTry 1st class free.\n\nNo previous J
 ewish learning required. Come as you are—and bring your questions.
LOCATION:Chabad Jewish Center of Petaluma
URL:https://www.jewishpetaluma.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7522546/je
 wish/The-Kabbalah-of-Meaning.htm
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T170000
UID:260914HlPO9lLLSEmdLFYddWRmNA
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present “Antarctica: The F
 rozen Desert\,” a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\, o
 pening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November.  T
 he exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after m
 ore than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity\,
  he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar regio
 ns. The exhibit features work generated over 6 voyages to the Antarctic Pe
 ninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Falklan
 ds and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photograph.\
 n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on Ear
 th\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely out
 side of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of year
 s ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 years. D
 efined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — vast
 \, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a kind
  of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever before
 .
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T163000
UID:260909s8K9JkMCUUuFOci5OOhH5Q
DESCRIPTION:September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month. On Monday\, 
 Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person Senio
 r Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\, CA.
  The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.-4:3
 0 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming native 
 artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in the
 ir art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts. The
  artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, guest cur
 ator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·  
        Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\, cu
 ltural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry Edwar
 d Frank\, Yurok/Kashaya Pomo\, who will show paintings and work with Legos
  titled Mind Prison\,\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas \\(Nico
 \\) Vargas\, Kashia Band of Pomo Indians\, whose art was featured at the 5
 5th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carretero\; 
 Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\, Kash
 ia Band of Pomo Indians\; Angelica Smith\, Manchester Point Arena and Yoka
 yo Rancheria\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\, Kashia Ba
 nd of Pomo Indians\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaugh\; Katie Wi
 lliams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, Big Valley Pomo Tribe.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
